test-results.json
# The great-docs build directory is ephemeral: `great-docs build` recreates the whole of
# it (`_site/` plus the generated `reference/` pages) from `great-docs.yml` and
# `user_guide/` on every run.
/great-docs/
# The docs toolchain lives in its own environment on purpose -- see the `docs` task in
# `pyproject.toml` for why it is not in `.venv`.
/.venv-docs/
conformance/bench_results.json
# `python -m conformance --real` stages shallow clones of the OSS targets, their isolated
# venvs, the rustest wheels built for those interpreters, and per-run JSON reports here.
# Everything in it is reproducible from conformance/real/*.toml.
conformance/real/_work/

# The terminal recordings under `demos/` ARE tracked: the documentation build reads them,
# and re-recording is a deliberate `poe demos` step rather than something CI does. See
# `demos/README.md`.

# SDD scratch (git-ignored)
.superpowers/

# SDD artifacts (kept in git history, not in the tree)
docs/superpowers/
